<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
    Venue B POS - saleable GOODS (product.template)
    ============================================================
    Odoo 19.0 Community. ADDITIVE only. Stable xmlids prefixed
    "atlas_pos_seed.".

    These are the physical articles sold over the counter: gala/evening
    dresses, suits/costumes, general clothing and accessories.

    === CRITICAL v19 PRODUCT FIELD RULES (do not regress) ===
      * type:  in Odoo 19 product.template.type has EXACTLY three valid
               values -> 'consu' (Goods), 'service' (Service), 'combo'.
               Physical goods = 'consu'.
               There is NO 'product'/'storable' value and the old
               'detailed_type' field DOES NOT EXIST in v19 - referencing
               either would crash the install.
      * is_storable: separate Boolean ("Track Inventory"). Omitted here -
               these are one-off gala dresses/suits; the shop does not run
               perpetual stock. (It is auto-forced False for non-'consu'
               anyway.) Left unset = no inventory tracking, which is what
               a made-to-measure tailor wants.
      * available_in_pos: defaults to False, so it MUST be set True
               explicitly on every product that should appear on the till.
      * pos_categ_ids: Many2many to pos.category (PLURAL). Set with the
               (6,0,[...]) command. The singular pos_categ_id does NOT
               exist in v19.
      * categ_id: the internal product.category (see product_category.xml).

    === TAX (Dutch BTW 21%) ===
      taxes_id is deliberately OMITTED on every product so each one
      INHERITS the company's default Sales Tax. For this Dutch-registered
      company that default must be "21% BTW (hoog)". In NL, both clothing
      and tailoring labour are taxed at the 21% standard rate, so 21%
      applies to the entire Venue B catalogue - no 9% or 0% line anywhere.

      We do NOT hard-code a tax xmlid (e.g. l10n_nl.btw_21): in v19 the
      Dutch taxes are per-company records addressed as
      account.<company_id>_btw_21, NOT a static global xmlid, so a static
      ref would not resolve on this blind DB and would crash the install.
      Inheriting the company default is the safe, blind-build-correct choice.
      => ONE-TIME ADMIN CHECK after install: confirm the company default
         Sales Tax = 21% BTW (Accounting > Configuration > Settings >
         Default Taxes). Every product below then gets 21% automatically.

    Prices are EUR placeholders; the owner can adjust them in the UI.

    noupdate="0": module-owned seed catalogue, safe to re-assert on upgrade.
-->
<odoo>
